title: FirstLoopDeniz


---

There’s a person sitting by the water’s edge, all by themselves. They don’t notice you, but the adorable little white dog beside them wags its tail when you approach. 
You don’t remember there being many dogs in Solster, is it an import?
Finally, the person looks up. You’ve seen them only a few times before, so their name escapes you.. But they were one of Dmitriy’s friends, you’re sure.

//<<if DoesHeKnow("DenizKnown") == true>>
	//Then, you remember. This is who the doctor mentioned before, wasn’t it? Deniz Cansel.
	//<<endif>>
-> Who are you?
	Sasha: "Who are you?"
	Deniz: “Deniz.”
	They eye you for a moment, as if waiting for you to react in a certain way when they tell you your name. When you don’t, they just look away.
-> Hello.
	Sasha: "Hello."
	They nod in greeting, waiting for you to say more. It's a little awkward.

-> What’s your dog’s name?
	Deniz: “She’s not mine.”
	-> Then whose is it?
		Sasha: "Then whose is it?"
		Deniz: “I don’t wanna talk about it.”
		-> What?
			Sasha: "What?"
			Deniz: “God is a bootlicker.”
				-> What???
					Sasha: "What??"
				-> Excuse me?
					Sasha: "Excuse me?"
				-> Checks out.
					Sasha: "Checks out."
		->Got it.
			Sasha: "Got it."
	-> Oh, okay.
		Sasha: "Oh, okay."
-> Are you a doctor?
	You’ve noted their garb, half a medical coat, half a trenchcoat. It’s an almost horrifying mismatch of fabrics. You’d be grossed out, if it wasn’t such spectacular fashion design.
	They notice you looking, their eyes darting over your body in return as a quick once-over before they nod as an answer.
Deniz: “Do you need something?”
-> Why are you sitting all the way out here?
	Sasha: "Why are you sitting all the way out here?"
	They shrug, the move long and languid. As if they’re trying to very unsubtly show their disinterest in the conversation. 
	<<if $PsychMajor == true>>
		They probably just came here to sit alone.
	<<endif>>
	-> Gotcha.
	-> See you around.
-> Nope, sorry for bothering.

===
